{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "kind": "otel-audit",
  "meta": {
    "audit_id": "python-flask-basic-20261119",
    "service_name": "python-flask-basic",
    "commit": "unavailable (not a Git checkout)",
    "language": "python",
    "framework": "Flask",
    "date": "2026-11-19",
    "status": "Partial",
    "genai_ownership_detected": false
  },
  "summary": [
    "Three findings cover the telemetry foundation, HTTP request visibility and local application logs.",
    "The source defines six API operations, plus Flask-generated HEAD and OPTIONS methods; request and shutdown warnings already exist.",
    "Initialize a shared service identity and reliable provider lifecycle, then add route traces and request latency/error/concurrency measurements.",
    "Export each application warning once to local logs, preserve stderr and keep the final shutdown warning ahead of logger teardown.",
    "All three findings are app-owned and selectable; no external prerequisite or manual telemetry decision blocks source work. Select findings and copy the generated $otel-instrument command."
  ],
  "flow": "audit -> select -> instrument -> verify -> configure/dashboard -> publish",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "check": "Manifest",
      "finding": "Python >=3.11; Flask >=3.1 is the only declared dependency; project version 0.1.0. No OTel packages or lockfile.",
      "source": "pyproject.toml:1-11"
    },
    {
      "check": "Entry point",
      "finding": "Flask CLI discovers app:app; app is created at module import. Six route functions and signal/atexit hooks are the entire application.",
      "source": "app.py:1-80"
    },
    {
      "check": "Route source",
      "finding": "GET /health, GET /tasks, GET /tasks/<int:task_id>, POST /tasks, PATCH /tasks/<int:task_id>, DELETE /tasks/<int:task_id>. Flask adds HEAD for GET and OPTIONS for all three path patterns; all are enumerated below.",
      "source": "app.py:32-80"
    },
    {
      "check": "Runtime/startup",
      "finding": "make dev runs uv sync then uv run flask run --port 8000 --reload. No Python minor pin, lock, tests, CI, env profile, container or OTel preload. uv sync would install/change state, so was not run. Safe future checks: uv run python -m compileall app.py and credential-free subprocess HTTP tests after dependencies are authorized.",
      "source": "Makefile:1-10; pyproject.toml:5-11"
    },
    {
      "check": "GenAI ownership",
      "finding": "No",
      "source": "app.py:1-80; pyproject.toml:1-11"
    },
    {
      "check": "Trace provider topology",
      "finding": "no provider: no OTel import, lazy helper, registration, exporter or external bootstrap reachable from the Flask CLI. Span inventory empty. Source scan and bundled AST scanner agree; installed environment and emission were not tested.",
      "source": "app.py:1-80; Makefile:6-7; .observe/evidence/python-otel-topology.json"
    },
    {
      "check": "Metric provider topology",
      "finding": "no provider: no custom/automatic metric registration or exporter. Metric inventory empty independently of trace status.",
      "source": "app.py:1-80; .observe/evidence/python-otel-topology.json"
    },
    {
      "check": "Log provider topology",
      "finding": "no provider; classification not configured. Existing app.logger.warning at request and signal-driven shutdown; no OTLP bridge, correlation, exporter or explicit operator opt-out in repository.",
      "source": "app.py:16-29,51-58; Makefile:6-7"
    },
    {
      "check": "Log formatting and sinks",
      "finding": "Application messages are constant. No custom formatter/filter/adapter or handler exists in app source. Proposed Flask release default handler formats timestamp/level/module/message to wsgi.errors or stderr; root handler availability affects its installation. Framework exception logging and Werkzeug request-line formatting need final export redaction tests; currently installed dependency behavior is not proven.",
      "source": "app.py:24,57; .observe/evidence/flask-3.1.3-flask_logging.py.txt"
    },
    {
      "check": "Local receiver resolution",
      "finding": "No configured OTLP signal/generic endpoints, launch env or advertised Studio tool available. Live local receiver and concrete Studio availability unverified. Only if no endpoint is configured/discovered at instrumentation time, conventional HTTP fallback http://127.0.0.1:4318, http/protobuf with /v1/traces, /v1/metrics, /v1/logs; gRPC alternative 127.0.0.1:4317 is unselected. Preserve explicit non-default ports; fixture port 14318 is a test destination, not discovered infrastructure.",
      "source": "Makefile:1-10; .observe/evidence/source-scan.json"
    },
    {
      "check": "Resource precedence",
      "finding": "No Resource or operator launch settings in source. Proposed defaults service.name=python-flask-basic, service.version=0.1.0; preserve OTEL_SERVICE_NAME and OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES and omit unknown environment/cloud metadata.",
      "source": "pyproject.toml:2-5; Makefile:6-7"
    },
    {
      "check": "Incident scope",
      "finding": "API request outcomes, input parse/shape errors, in-flight requests, release identity and graceful shutdown are app-owned. No external client, database, worker, queue, scheduled freshness obligation, authentication, stream, AI, canary or deployment autoscaling surface exists. Health returns a static status; changing its readiness semantics is product work outside this audit. No incident artifacts were supplied.",
      "source": "app.py:1-80; .observe/evidence/source-scan.json"
    },
    {
      "check": "Detection and localization",
      "finding": "Proposed http.server.request.duration histogram count, latency and status distribution are MTTD-improving inputs; http.server.active_requests measures concurrent pressure, not a capacity policy. Route spans and correlated logs localize an already-observed fault. Platform host saturation/restarts have no owner configuration here and are not fabricated app findings.",
      "source": "app.py:32-80"
    },
    {
      "check": "Package compatibility (2026-11-19)",
      "finding": "Latest inspected metadata-compatible proposed set: API/SDK/HTTP OTLP exporter 1.45.2 with Flask and logging instrumentations 0.66b2, shared semconv/instrumentation dependencies 0.66b2; Python >=3.10 package requirement fits project >=3.11, Flask instrumentor accepts Flask >=1.0 and project >=3.1 permits current 3.1.3. SDK requires API==1.45.2 and semconv==0.66b2; exporter requires SDK~=1.45.2. No lock or conflicting OTel constraints. Full resolver/runtime compatibility remains downstream; no packages installed. Official metadata URLs, release dates and SHA256 receipts are in evidence.",
      "source": ".observe/evidence/package-compatibility-20261119.json; pyproject.toml:5-8"
    },
    {
      "check": "Official HTTP guidance",
      "finding": "Proposed Flask instrumentor supports route-named spans and HTTP duration/active metrics. Inspect exact release wheel recorded in evidence; use stable HTTP opt-in before initialization. Official docs: https://opentelemetry-python-contrib.readthedocs.io/en/latest/instrumentation/flask/flask.html and https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/http/http-metrics/ (reviewed 2026-11-19).",
      "source": ".observe/evidence/opentelemetry-instrumentation-flask-0.66b2-opentelemetry_instrumentation_flask___init__.py.txt"
    },
    {
      "check": "Official logging guidance",
      "finding": "Inspected published logging wheel 0.66b2: LoggingInstrumentor gets global LoggerProvider and installs one contrib handler by default; inject_trace_context is supported; handler flush creates a thread. Avoid deprecated SDK handler overlap and explicitly honor OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=none in source-owned setup. Official docs: https://opentelemetry-python-contrib.readthedocs.io/en/latest/instrumentation/logging/logging.html (reviewed 2026-11-19).",
      "source": ".observe/evidence/opentelemetry-instrumentation-logging-0.66b2-opentelemetry_instrumentation_logging___init__.py.txt; .observe/evidence/opentelemetry-instrumentation-logging-0.66b2-opentelemetry_instrumentation_logging_handler.py.txt"
    },
    {
      "check": "Audit execution boundary",
      "finding": "Read source and official metadata/wheel files; ran bundled static Python topology scanner. Did not start the application, execute telemetry, install packages, change launch settings or query cloud resources. Source digests recorded; Git commit unavailable.",
      "source": ".observe/evidence/source-scan.json; .observe/evidence/python-otel-topology.json"
    }
  ],
